│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue. After careful analysis  │
│ of the provided code context, the root cause appears to be how     │
│ sphinx.ext.autodoc handles docstrings for type aliases.            │
│ Specifically, it seems to be falling back to the default "alias    │
│ of..." description instead of using the multi-line docstrings      │
│ defined within the type alias declarations. This is likely due to  │
│ a limitation in how autodoc processes these specific types of      │
│ docstrings.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The solution is to explicitly instruct autodoc to use the          │
│ multi-line docstrings. We can achieve this by adding a custom      │
│ directive to the sphinx.ext.autodoc configuration. This will force │
│ autodoc to parse and render the multi-line docstrings correctly.   │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the reasoning and the patch:                                │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that sphinx.ext.autodoc isn't correctly interpreting  │
│ the multi-line docstrings defined for the type aliases.  A simple  │
│ fix is to add a directive that tells autodoc to always use the     │
│ full docstring, regardless of the type. This will ensure that the  │
│ intended descriptions are displayed in the generated API           │
│ documentation.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
