│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core problem is that the       │
│ sphinx.ext.autodoc extension isn’t correctly processing the        │
│ docstrings for type aliases, resulting in the default “alias of…”  │
│ text being displayed instead of the custom docstrings. This is     │
│ likely due to how autodoc handles type hints and the way it        │
│ renders documentation. The provided code context suggests a        │
│ configuration issue within conf.py related to autodoc.             │
│ Specifically, the extensions list needs to explicitly include      │
│ sphinx.ext.autodoc to ensure it’s enabled.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Here’s the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
